1
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:29,897
Every time the rain no longer falls, and I
see the sky, I think the rain is falling.

2
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,277
Back to when I was a child.

3
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:34,937
Who could only cry?

4
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:37,497
Blindly chasing after him.

5
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:42,317
I fell far behind my only thought.

6
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,377
One day I will be stronger!

7
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,897
Bridery and gratitude.

8
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:50,497
Fading with the wind.

9
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,337
Am I stronger now than I was before?

10
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,297
Or as weak as back then?

11
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:57,397
I don't know for sure.

12
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:01,157
But until I do, my voyage will not end.

13
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:06,360
No matter what's next, I'm
walking straight ahead.

14
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:12,577
So let's go, there's nothing
that can stop us now!

15
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:17,560
Though time's all on our side,
we'll never let it pull us down.

16
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:22,577
And we may fall, but we'll
always keep on standing.

17
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:27,180
There's no way anything
will take what I hope.

18
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:33,677
The voices inside me push
me to keep surviving.

19
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:39,257
I'll go on, I'll get through,
no matter what I gotta do.

20
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:43,177
The fiercest storms of
all can pour upon me.

21
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:48,380
I don't care why in the
world would I turn back?

22
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:54,817
So let's go,

23
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:56,980
there's nothing that can stop!

24
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:02,920
The times that are on our side
will never let it pull us down.

25
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:07,897
And we may fall, but we'll
always keep on standing.

26
00:02:07,980 --> 00:02:14,097
There's no way anything will take
what I hold dear away from me.

27
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,740
I know the future's there for us to see.

28
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:29,620
What is that?

29
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,841
It looks like a tunnel of flames!

30
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:35,777
Ever since you were little, you've
never listened to a word I said.

31
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:36,690
Have you?

32
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:42,613
Then you run off and do something crazy.

33
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:50,540
Like old times. Huh, Luffy?

34
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:59,020
Let's go!

35
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:25,340
That's Firefist Ace!

36
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:28,060
He's free!

37
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,270
Yee-haw!

38
00:03:31,353 --> 00:03:33,020
You did a Straw Hat! Yeah!

39
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,220
You can suck it, baby!

40
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:39,055
He hasn't slowed down once
after all he's been through.

41
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:41,660
You can't stop this guy!

42
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:44,160
Your papa would be so proud!

43
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,940
See that?

44
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,420
He really did it!

45
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,900
That crazy little bastard saved Ace!

46
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:54,220
Of course he did.

47
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,177
After all, he's Luffy.

48
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:57,880
Keep your cool!

49
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:00,220
This isn't over yet!

50
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:03,040
Open fire as soon as they land! Sir!

51
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,720
Let's split up for now!

52
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:09,220
Don't let your guard down yet! Okay!

53
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:11,460
Wait, no!

54
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,320
Flame Commandment!

55
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,090
Fire!

56
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,580
They're strong! Be careful, men!

57
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:44,840
Can you still fight, Luffy?

58
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:46,520
Of course I can't!

59
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:50,540
Luffy! Ace!

60
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:56,177
Remember, Ace is a Logia Titan, so
he's going to be really tough to hit.

61
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:59,157
Never thought I'd need my
little brother to save me.

62
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,500
Guess I'll swallow my pride this time.

63
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:03,175
I owe you one, Luffy.

64
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:10,456
Thanks, but I sure couldn't have done
it if Whitebeard hadn't shown up.

65
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:12,921
You think we'll let you get away?

66
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:18,027
Consider this your
execution ground, pirates!

67
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,637
That's my little brother
you're trying to murder.

68
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,367
I'll have to ask you to stop

69
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,040
You're dead

70
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:02,053
This is fun and all, but the sooner
we leave this dump, the better, right?

71
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:09,100
They're a fine team, I dare say.

72
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:10,597
We're pulling out!

73
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,510
Clear a path!

74
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:18,300
We can't let them get away!

75
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:23,590
Firefly!

76
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,060
Fire it off!

77
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:31,460
This isn't over yet execute them both

78
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:59,378
I've got to admit, you've
gotten pretty tough, Luffy.

79
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:11,420
One of these days, I'll
be stronger than you.

80
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,420
All right, then I'll handle
things in the meantime.

81
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:21,860
What a pain.

82
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,837
All right, ice block.

83
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,700
Stand back, Luffy.

84
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:32,040
And now, Pheasant Beak!

85
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,200
Flame Mirror!

86
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,574
You're all right, sir?

87
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:59,336
This is the worst blunder of my life.

88
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,920
We have to rectify this.

89
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,100
Huh, just let him go.

90
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:07,117
It makes things more interesting.

91
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,030
I say

92
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,480
Cut the crap

93
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:13,277
Those guys went toe-to-toe
with an admiral.

94
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:17,060
What the hell are we supposed
to do pull yourselves together?

95
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:20,640
Admiral Sakazuki

96
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:24,297
They won't make it out of here alive.

97
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:25,262
Don't you worry

98
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:27,830
mr.

99
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:33,317
two i hope i could honor
your memory in my own humble

100
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:37,597
way anywho that's enough
heroism For a lifetime I'm

101
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:42,737
leaving what Splatoon is
this traitor from no hold on

102
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:47,080
he's a prisoner Impersonating
a guard no I was too slow

103
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:56,857
The enemy ship is coming
through On land somehow Don't

104
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:59,877
get close It's running on
the ground with his paddles

105
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:02,500
Wait, who's on board? I can't see.

106
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:06,197
It's Squared.

107
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:09,162
And it looks like he's
got his crew with him too.

108
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:13,057
Make a break for it, Pops!

109
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,157
We'll guard you.

110
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:18,460
We'll show those bastards the
pride of the spider world pirates!

111
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,337
God damn it!

112
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:25,714
What are you thinking?

113
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:37,997
Don't be an idiot squad!

114
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,077
You'll die!

115
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:41,513
Yeah, you got a death wish or something!

116
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:45,910
Yes.

117
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,102
Yes, of course.

118
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:52,538
After what I did to Pops,
this is the least I can do.

119
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,720
I can't hope to atone for my crime.

120
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:04,942
But if I don't die fighting here,
I know I'll never rest in peace.

121
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:09,839
I'm sorry for bringing you with me.

122
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:12,820
This should be my fight. What?

123
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,837
Are you kidding me?

124
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,237
We wanted to follow you.

125
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,657
Yeah, you're our captain,
to the bitter end.

126
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:20,269
If we all die here,
then that's our choice.

127
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:22,157
Let's not get sentimental here.

128
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,711
Lead the charge, captain.

129
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,350
Thank you.

130
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:30,860
Everyone else grab Ace
and make a run for it.

131
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:34,260
Saint Helmer's Fire!

132
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:40,260
Those fools.

133
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:43,460
Squared, no.

134
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:47,857
Oh, you think anyone's going to
be happy with a plan like this?

135
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:50,528
Hey, hurry up and get
these cuffs off of me!

136
00:10:58,360 --> 00:10:59,380
What the hell?

137
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:01,169
Did we run into something?

138
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,440
But why, Pops?

139
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:21,157
You believe you've done me a favor?

140
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,617
You poor, selfish child!

141
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:29,697
Don't you know how cruel it is to
force a father to bury his own sons?

142
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:33,497
And show some humility!

143
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:37,517
You think I'm on my last legs
because of one measly poke?

144
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:40,477
It was settled long before I came here.

145
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:43,677
Everyone has to grow old and die someday.

146
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:50,760
Our

147
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,457
business is done.

148
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:55,777
Pull out now,

149
00:11:55,860 --> 00:12:00,277
and I'll stay here to make sure I don't
lose any more of my boys to these bastards!

150
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,437
You're staying?

151
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:02,640
What do you mean?

152
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,637
Listen up, White Beard Pirates!

153
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:11,360
And listen well!

154
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:18,057
These are my final orders as your captain!

155
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:20,197
So you better follow them!

156
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,677
You're kidding, right?

157
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,837
That's the last thing we want to hear!

158
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:25,777
We're going back together! Yeah!

159
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:27,477
We can't go on without you!

160
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:30,377
We didn't save Ace to let our captain die!

161
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:33,217
Crossfire!

162
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:35,817
Let's go!

163
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:39,177
Even family must part ways now and then!

164
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,957
You must survive!

165
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:43,097
Return to the New World!

166
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:46,080
Continue your legacy without me!

167
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:55,390
No!

168
00:12:55,473 --> 00:12:56,303
You can't die!

169
00:12:56,386 --> 00:12:57,960
We can find another way!

170
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:01,897
Make no mistake!

171
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:04,617
I'm a relic of a bygone era!

172
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:10,980
Long have I sailed, but no ship
can carry me into the new age.

173
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:21,160
Now go and forge your own path!

174
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,200
There's no way we can leave you here.

175
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,837
Look, I know how you
feel, but it's an order.

176
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,000
Hulk, I know. What are you?

177
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,820
Don't look back, boys.

178
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,060
A new age is coming.

179
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:01,057
Oh, man, what a hole!

180
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:04,777
Hey, you don't even care
about treasure, you weirdo!

181
00:14:04,860 --> 00:14:06,177
Come check it out.

182
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:08,117
There's plenty to go around, buddy.

183
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:11,380
Forget it, he's always like this. Huh?

184
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:12,836
What does that mean?

185
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:15,837
We wouldn't even have these
treasures without him!

186
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:18,660
Well, what are you looking for then?

187
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,230
Hey!

188
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,853
You listening, Newgate?

189
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:28,600
It's been a long journey, but a good one.

190
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:36,580
Let's finally put an end to this.

191
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:43,617
The rainforest's falling apart!

192
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,540
Somebody stop Whitebeard!

193
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,190
Damn!

194
00:14:49,273 --> 00:14:52,298
At this rate, he's gonna
bring down the whole island!

195
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:54,900
We came here as a family!

196
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,767
We should leave as one, too!

197
00:14:56,900 --> 00:14:57,730
Yeah!

198
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:59,060
Pops, come with us!

199
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:04,020
You mean to disobey your captain's order?

200
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,620
I told you fools to get away!

201
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,030
Alright!

202
00:15:08,113 --> 00:15:09,237
This might be our only chance!

203
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,320
Hit Wipe here with all you've got!

204
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:18,920
I won't do it!

205
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:22,577
Hey, come on, we're better
off doing what Pops says.

206
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:23,640
Are you crazy?

207
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:24,857
Pops is our father!

208
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:26,257
I won't leave him here to die!

209
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:27,170
I know!

210
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:28,460
Don't be stupid!

211
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:31,980
Do you think any of us want
Dial Pops behind? Move!

212
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:35,477
Bickering about your own petty
feelings at a time like this,

213
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,837
that's the kind of stuff
Pops wouldn't stand for!

214
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:41,214
Can't you see that he's trying
to do what's best for us?

215
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:45,570
Sorry.

216
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:52,340
Everyone get back on the ships!

217
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:54,740
Hey, Ace!

218
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:10,520
Come on! Hurry it up!

219
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,112
We're about to take off!

220
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,780
Commander Marco, let's head back!

221
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,250
Pops.

222
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:30,200
He no longer has to worry
about saving firefish days.

223
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:31,820
Admiral, sir?

224
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:36,940
So long as his men can escape, he'll
sink Marineford and all of us with it.

225
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:40,780
He's prepared to die, I've no doubt.

226
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:43,360
Vice Admiral Garp, you okay?

227
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:46,280
Whitebeard thinks our era is over?

228
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:49,100
Yeah, the old man is probably right.

229
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,717
We still don't know what
happened to Whitebeard.

230
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,094
What about his allies?

231
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,317
Did he really sell them out or what?

232
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,230
Perfect.

233
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:59,937
How am I supposed to write
a story on the battle now?

234
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:01,657
What's wrong with their snails?

235
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:03,152
We don't go out all day!

236
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,350
Really?

237
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:08,124
That piece of crap is
still hiding in its shell?

238
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:09,180
Come on!

239
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,440
Get back out here, Mr. Snail.

240
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:12,817
We still need your help.

241
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:15,429
Captain Buggy's ready
to defeat Whitebeard.

242
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,737
Don't they realize what they're saying?

243
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:20,897
Yeah, Whitebeard's wounded, but
he's tearing down buildings.

244
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:22,451
Just look at the bastard.

245
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:25,133
Why'd I have to go and say I'd beat him?

246
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:27,737
These morons believe
anything you tell them.

247
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:29,938
It's their fault for feeding my ego.

248
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:32,057
I can't help it! Lure it out!

249
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:36,477
We gotta showcase Captain Buggy's
awesomeness for the entire world to see.

250
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:37,740
Bring it over here.

251
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,744
I'll just smash the shell open.

252
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,380
Yeah, one strong pound ought to do it.

253
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:45,229
Quit messing with the
paw thing, you fools.

254
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:48,631
The transponder snail came out on its own.

255
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:49,930
Come on,

256
00:17:50,013 --> 00:17:52,017
we're starting the broadcast and make sure

257
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:54,806
you capture the moment
that I kill Whitebeard.

258
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,640
Hey, look. It's bad.

259
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:01,518
Transponder snail, go down a little.

260
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:06,220
Why, hello everybody!

261
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:08,460
Time for Captain Buggy!

262
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,280
This guy again?

263
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,840
Get to the sea! Now!

264
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:15,877
Hurry up and get on the ships!

265
